  "body": "## Result\n\nConditional **\u03ba = 0.001675608585476885** (exact `335121717095377/200000000000000000`).\n\n- Over #1169 (`0.001675568675201533`): **+3.9910275352e-8**, i.e. **0.0023819%**.\n- Over #1148 (`0.001675560947524449`): +4.76e-8.\n- Conservative endpoint: `0.001675608582632503`.\n\n## Construction\n\nThe base is #1169: #1148's joint entrance groups 603/611/635 with an exact T37 owner flow. This PR adds one ingredient to it: jeremykothe2's width-neutral eighth triangle-hybrid slot **X54/E589** (holders 335, 367) from #1130.\n\n- **Recipe.** The edits and frames are identical to `RECIPE-X54-ends7.json`, rebased onto `k8-joint-entrances/FULL-WORD.json.gz` (content `1f666402\u2026`). The joint-entrance recipe changes only frames, and none of its 39 changed B frames lies on an X54 position.\n- **Local profile.** It goes from `{1:2364,2:498,3:412,4:130,5:82,8:8}` to `{1:2364,2:498,3:414,4:126,5:84,8:8}`, a change of `{3:+2, 4:\u22124, 5:+2}`. The width inventory `{4:44,5:44,7:38,8:114,9:240}` is unchanged.\n- **Reused from #1169 unchanged:**\n  - the 159,840 whole-helper roles in 333 calls;\n  - the owner map and pattern flow;\n  - the windows and parent geometry;\n  - idle `{1:834,48:11374}`.\n- **Provider identity.** This is the only new identity. It is rebound name-by-name (15 identities) to a fresh native replay of the new word, and the SPEC is re-frozen through the unchanged discovery/freeze path.\n- **Ceiling.** #1148's all-T signed-dual bound, pinned to the X54 plan, gives a grid ceiling of exactly `0.001675608585476885`. The construction attains the fixed-family ceiling for this local word and inventory.\n\nThe global profile is `{1:788046,2:165834,3:137862,4:41958,5:27972,8:2664,48:11374}`, with live stock 33,152 and deficit 11,840.\n\n## Validation (passed)\n\n- **Local audit.** The independent exact local audit of the X54 word passes on all 704 columns in both orientations (`PASS_INDEPENDENT_EXACT_FORWARD_AND_DUAL_ENDPOINT_FRAMES_ENTRANCES_CONES`).\n- **Local controls.**\n  - #1148's 27 entrance controls.\n  - NewBArch's slot controls: C0, the recipe, and four mutants, run globally and for X=54. All 10 outcomes are as pinned.\n- **Native replay.** A fresh five-stage native replay of the new word.\n- **Strict T37 admission** with the retained #1129 engines:\n  - bind, emit, audit, invoice and assembly;\n  - 69 admission and 12 bit controls;\n  - the independent owner checker with 7 controls;\n  - all 47 outer inequalities;\n  - result: `PASS_STRICT_T37_THREE_DEMOTIONS 0.001675608585476885`.\n- **Fixed-family upper bound.** `PASS_ALL_T_K8_JOINT_X54_SIGNED_DUAL_UPPER_RELAXATION 0.001675608585476885`.\n\nReceipts are in `research/joint-x54-t37/evidence/`. The package `verify.py` chains all of the above from the pinned sibling #1169 layout. Along the way it rebuilds the owner table and plan, rebinds the provider from the fresh native replay, and checks that every reproduced artifact matches.\n\n```sh\npython -B research/joint-x54-t37/verify.py --work /absolute/new/output-directory\n```\n\nThis needs Python 3.11+, a C++ compiler and Boost headers. It uses no network and no solver.\n\nThe branch sits on #1169's head `13d02293`. It reuses these files from that package, pinned in `SOURCE-PINS.json`:\n\n- `upstream-layout.tar.gz`\n- `construct.py`\n- `PATTERN-FLOW.json`\n- `OWNERS.json.gz`\n- `GLOBAL-TEMPLATE.json.gz`\n\n## Scope\n\nThis is a conditional finite construction. These obligations remain:\n\n- all-size compiler;\n- common-label and mutable-source realization;\n- whole-call hosting;\n- precision and tape;\n- exact recovery;\n- analytic transfer;\n- the PR559 recurrence correction;\n- PR589 bit H1\u2013H5.\n\nNo unconditional theorem, full formalization or global packing optimality is claimed.\n\n## Credit\n\n- #1130 (jeremykothe2): the X54 recipe.\n- NewBArch: the triangle-hybrid builder and controls, vendored byte-for-byte.\n- #1148 (Thomas DiFiore/Codex) and its local ancestry.\n- #1169: the T37 owner flow and packaging.\n- #1129 (Ali Romman/Codex): integer flow, matching and T37 audit.\n- #1131: wave order.\n- #942, #795 and #890: the dual all-T bound.\n- #589: the unchanged bit supplier.\n\nNew composition by Rohan Arun with AI assistance (Claude). Apache-2.0; all original notices are retained.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TGoMCHAqctZe4wTb4Qr7VV\n",
